NAME
       proptest - print and set display-manager object properties

SYNOPSIS
       proptest [options]
       proptest [options] object-id object-type property-id value

DESCRIPTION
       Every mode-setting object -- connector, CRTC, plane -- carries a set of
       named  properties,  and  that  is  where most of what can be configured
       about the display actually lives: the power state of a  connector,  its
       EDID  blob,  the gamma table of a CRTC, the source and destination rec-
       tangles of a plane.

       In its first form proptest prints all of  them,  with  each  property's
       type,  its  permitted  range or enumeration, and its current value.  In
       its second form it sets one.

       Setting a property needs the node's master rights, so  it  fails  while
       another program -- an X server, say -- holds them.  Printing does not.

OPTIONS
       -D device
              Open the given device node instead of searching.

       -M module
              Open  the  node  belonging  to  the  named  driver, for instance
              vmwgfx.

OPERANDS
       object-type
              One of connector, crtc, or plane.

       object-id
              The numeric id of the object, as printed by the first form or by
              modetest(1).

       property-id
              The numeric id of the property, likewise.

       value  The new value: a number, or the numeric member  of  an  enumera-
              tion.

SEE ALSO
       drminfo(1), modetest(1), vbltest(1)

